'''Brazil 6–5 Poland''' was a [[association football|football]] match held during the [[1938 FIFA World Cup]] in France and still remembered by many Polish fans as [[Poland national football team|Poland]]'s first ever FIFA World Cup match. It is also [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]]'s highest-scoring match in a FIFA World Cup tournament. The match held the record for the highest-scoring World Cup match until [[1954 FIFA World Cup|1954]], when [[Austria national football team|Austria]] beat [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]] [[Austria v Switzerland (1954 FIFA World Cup)|7–5]]. 

__TOC__

